# The bank $A5 guard's (kind $08) pieces no play reaches, from the first
# level's state, where record $092B is the guard (stopped, $07 0, code
# word $E5B8).
# GuardPlacedHold ($A5:F00E), GuardStart's start for $07 = 11: the
# record put back to state $0C (+0) with $07 = $0B (+7); the actor loop
# starts it again by its kind's table.
load build/aladdin/states/level1.state
wait 10
poke 00092B 0C
poke 000932 0B
wait 60
# GuardGiveUp ($A5:E794): its code word ($03) set to $E794, as GuardChase
# sets it when the player is far off; the actor loop resumes it there.
load build/aladdin/states/level1.state
wait 10
poke 00092E 94,E7
wait 180
# Again with $141C set for its first frames (it waits while that or
# $1427 is set), then cleared: it is put where the player is, and waits
# while ACTOR_09 bit 6 is set; its x then set to $0700, off the view, so
# that bit clears and it comes back facing the player and leaps.
load build/aladdin/states/level1.state
wait 10
poke 00141C 01
poke 00092E 94,E7
wait 8
poke 00141C 00
wait 4
poke 000937 00,07
wait 120
# PlayerSceneRuns ($A5:EB31) past its hold: in stage a1 s0 the figure
# ($092B, $07 1, x $0B40) stands at spot $1C waiting for the player's x
# to reach $0B00, which play from that state does not do. The player's x
# set to $0B10 with the play field's scroll x ($1773) at $0A80 (the
# player is kept within 16-240 pixels of it). The figure runs on 72
# frames, rears and jumps, then waits for its x + $20 to be below the
# player's: at frame 450 the player's x set to $0BC0 and the scroll to
# $0B00. It leaps, lands and starts over as way 0 (GuardRestart, then
# the guard's own walk of 40 frames and GuardStop).
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a1_s0.state
wait 30
poke 001773 80,0A
poke 0008E7 10,0B
wait 420
poke 001773 00,0B
poke 0008E7 C0,0B
wait 300
# GuardRestart's table for $07 = 4 (PlayerSceneDropIn) and 12 (shown at
# once, then the guard's own walk): the level-1 guard put back to state
# $0C with each.
# The walk's frames after its first BRK ($A5:E5A0) run only when the
# loop does not call the guard's wait routine after that BRK: GuardWait
# (state 1, $146B cleared by the restart) always sends it on at once.
# The loop calls it only with ACTOR_09 bit 7 set, which GuardStart sets.
# So the guard is resumed at GuardRestart by its code word ($E554, as
# kind $69's end sends the escort) with $07 0 and ACTOR_09 $50 (bit 7
# clear, as GuardGiveUp leaves it): it walks its 40 frames, then stops.
load build/aladdin/states/level1.state
wait 10
poke 000932 00
poke 000934 50
poke 00092E 54,E5
wait 60
load build/aladdin/states/level1.state
wait 10
poke 00092B 0C
poke 000932 04
wait 60
load build/aladdin/states/level1.state
wait 10
poke 00092B 0C
poke 000932 0C
wait 60
# GuardStop ($A5:E5B6) at an edge (the tile's behaviour bit 5: pose
# $16): no guard stops on one in play. In stage a1 s0 the tiles at x
# $0090-$00B0, y $01B0 have behaviour $23; the figure there ($092B) is
# put at x $00A0, y $01A8 (standing on them) and resumed at GuardStop by
# its code word ($E5B6, as GuardChase sends a guard).
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a1_s0.state
wait 10
poke 000937 A0,00
poke 00093A A8,01
poke 00092E B6,E5
wait 20
# GuardRun ($A5:E5E8) into a wall ($A5:E60B: on at GuardClimb): no guard
# runs at one in play. In stage a1 s0 the floor at y $01A0 meets a wall
# from x $03E0; the figure ($092B) put at x $03D9.80, y $0198, facing
# right (facing 0, flip 1), and resumed at GuardRun by its code word
# ($E5E8, as GuardChase sends a guard). Its first step ($1.80) takes it to
# x $03DB, where ActorOutOfWall8's probe meets the wall (from farther
# back, GuardStepAhead jumps it first).
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a1_s0.state
wait 10
poke 000936 80,D9,03
poke 00093A 98,01
poke 00093F 00,01
poke 00092E E8,E5
wait 120
# The same wall met in the air with G_BACK_OFF ($46) set ($A5:E6E6: on at
# GuardFlip): from x $03C8 GuardStepAhead jumps it into the wall.
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a1_s0.state
wait 10
poke 000937 C8,03
poke 00093A 98,01
poke 00093F 00,01
poke 000971 01
poke 00092E E8,E5
wait 60
# GuardJump rising with ActorSettleOnFloor meeting a tile whose behaviour
# has bit 3 (a slope's side) ($A5:E6C0: faced by it, on at GuardLand): in
# stage a1 s0 the tile at x $05B0, y $0180 has behaviour $0A; the figure
# put at x $05BE, y $018A, rising 2 pixels a frame (vertical speed
# $FFFE00) and moving left 3, and resumed at GuardJump by its code word
# ($E6A0): its probe 8 (5 to the side, 6 up) and its own x then fall in
# that tile.
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a1_s0.state
wait 10
poke 000937 BE,05
poke 00093A 8A,01
poke 000948 00,FE,FF
poke 00092E A0,E6
wait 60
# GuardRun's throw with no record free for its children ($A5:E698: none
# report, so the preset with none seen): from x $03C8 in stage a1 s0 the
# figure jumps, climbs the wall, turns back and runs off the edge; at
# frame 15 it waits at the throw's BRK. The free list's head ($15E4,
# $34 then) set negative for the next frame, when its three ActorSpawn
# calls all fail, then put back.
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a1_s0.state
wait 10
poke 000937 C8,03
poke 00093A 98,01
poke 00093F 00,01
poke 00092E E8,E5
wait 15
poke 0015E4 FE
wait 1
poke 0015E4 34
wait 30
